% year on year, and cancellations are below 1%. Backlog is not revenue, though. Conversion depends on production and delivery timing (source: vltg-orders-h1).\n- **Run-rate:** The last four quarters sum to C$3,735M (905 + 960 + 980 + 890). The 2027 guidance is therefore about 12% above that, which is in line with orders growth of 11%.\n- **Q2 2026 dip:** Q2 revenue fell to C$890M from C$980M in Q1. The cause was the nine-week fire shutdown of Halbrook, the largest plant (source: halbrook-fire).\n- **Halbrook recovery:** The plant restarted in August at full capacity. Management expects to recover the lost shipments by mid-2027. That deferred volume should add to H1 2027 revenue, which supports the guidance. It also puts catch-up pressure on the first half of 2027.\n\n**Risks:** Execution is the main one. Delivering C$4.2B needs about C$1.05B a quarter, against a best recent quarter of C$980M. That means roughly 7% growth over the best quarter, plus the Halbrook catch-up. A second plant incident, or slower recovery than management expects, would push revenue below guidance. Even so, the backlog gives about C$0.9B of cushion above guidance.\n\n**Estimate:** I put the central case at about C$4.1–4.2B. The downside is about C$3.9B if the catch-up is slow. The upside is limited by capacity, not demand.\n\n**Gaps:** I did not find Q3 2026 results or any other 2027 disclosures. I also did not check how much of the backlog is scheduled for delivery in 2027.","ttft_ms":1719,"type":"result","duration_ms":30158,"uuid":"53d8e3ea-2d7d-4852-8bb3-a079424852f1","ttft_stream_ms":1496,"time_to_request_ms":388,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":27,"system_prompt":20,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":23,"input_attachments":68,"input_hooks":9,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":36,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":56,"init_frame_send":15,"engine_pickup":3,"loop_entry":12,"message_prep":3,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":8,"request_announcements":83,"query_setup":1,"